{
  "id": "tah-geometry",
  "chapterNumber": "5",
  "title": {
    "en": "Geometry & Coordinate Geometry",
    "ar": null
  },
  "railLabel": {
    "en": "Geometry & Coordinates",
    "ar": "الهندسة والإحداثيات"
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Plane-geometry facts together with the coordinate toolkit: distance, midpoint, gradient, and the equation of a circle.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Points & shapes",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Distance \\( =\\sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^{2}+(y_2-y_1)^{2}} \\); midpoint is the average of coordinates; gradient \\( =\\tfrac{\\Delta y}{\\Delta x} \\). A circle centred at the origin is \\( x^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2} \\). Interior angles of an \\( n \\)-gon sum to \\( (n-2)180^{\\circ} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Distance",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sqrt{\\Delta x^{2}+\\Delta y^{2}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Midpoint",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\big(\\tfrac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\tfrac{y_1+y_2}{2}\\big) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Gradient",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{\\Delta y}{\\Delta x} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Circle",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( x^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 5.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Find the distance from \\( (0,0) \\) to \\( (3,4) \\). \\[ \\sqrt{3^{2}+4^{2}}=5. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 5.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Write the equation of a circle centred at the origin with radius \\( 5 \\). \\[ x^{2}+y^{2}=25. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "Practice Problem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Find the equation of the circle with centre \\((3,-2)\\) that passes through \\((7,1).\\) <details><summary>Show solution</summary><div>Radius \\(r=\\sqrt{(7-3)^2+(1+2)^2}=\\sqrt{16+9}=5.\\) Equation: \\((x-3)^2+(y+2)^2=25.\\)</div></details>",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
